	    ErrorCode : DINT;  //! <Type Comment="Error information&#13;&#10;0 .. no error occured&#13;&#10;-1 .. wrong profile status by the reverse start&#13;&#10;-2 .. no valid movement to be reconstructed&#13;&#10;-3 .. first reverse movement generation failed&#13;&#10;-4 .. first reverse movement generation failed (movement after transition movement where profile has stopped)&#13;&#10;-5 .. invalid movement specification recovered from user buffer&#13;&#10;-6 .. reverse movement generation from user buffer failed&#13;&#10;-7 .. assignments between profile buffer movements (which should have been overwritten) and their user buffer movements could not have been deleted&#13;&#10;-8 .. invalid pointer - SW error, movement sequence in profile buffer could not have been restored&#13;&#10;&gt;-19 &amp; &lt;-10 .. some error has occured and additionally error -8 (SW error, movement sequence in profile buffer could not have been restored). &#13;&#10;Error code is calculated as &quot;original error code -10&quot;; for example if first reverse movement generation failed (-3) and additionally movement sequence could not have been restored the error code would be: -3 -10 = -13&#13;&#10;-23 .. Assigning of the user buffer movement to the generated reverse movement failed during first reverse movement generation - see error code -3&#13;&#10;-24 .. Assigning of the user buffer movement to the generated reverse movement failed during first reverse movement generation (movement after transition movement where profile has stopped) - see error code -4&#13;&#10;-26 .. Assigning of the user buffer movement to the generated reverse movement failed during reverse movement generation from user buffer - see error code -6&#13;&#10;" Name="t_s_Reverse.ErrorCode"/>
